<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS hardened-runtime entitlements for the lets-chat desktop bundle.

  Tauri signs with the hardened runtime enabled, and under it a signed app
  needs the matching capability entitlement to reach a TCC-protected device
  API (camera, microphone, ...). These entitlements are inert until the
  codesign step runs, which only happens on the macOS build path owned by
  LC-126 (parked for lack of macOS hardware + Apple credentials). On
  Linux / Windows builds this file is ignored, and macOS is not yet in
  bundle.targets, so nothing consumes it today; it is wired into
  tauri.conf.json (bundle.macOS.entitlements) so the keys are in place when
  signing lands.

  LC-137: getDisplayMedia (screen share). There is NO codesign entitlement
  for screen capture. Screen recording is gated purely by TCC (the
  user-granted Screen Recording permission in System Settings, raised at
  runtime via CGRequestScreenCaptureAccess / the automatic first-use prompt);
  no entitlement and no Info.plist usage string controls it. So the
  screen-share slice adds nothing to the dict below. There is no real
  `com.apple.security.device.screen-capture` key - the earlier draft of this
  file invented one. See Apple's hardened-runtime entitlement list:
  https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/hardened-runtime
  The WebKit-layer getUserMedia consent is auto-granted by wry's UI delegate;
  whether WKWebView exposes getDisplayMedia at all, and whether that delegate
  also covers it, is unverified and must be confirmed during the LC-126 macOS
  bring-up (a getDisplayMedia call may still need a Rust-side hook).

  LC-134 (getUserMedia, camera + microphone) is what actually populates this
  file: it adds com.apple.security.device.camera and
  com.apple.security.device.audio-input. LC-126 may add the remaining signing
  entitlements WebKit needs under the hardened runtime (e.g.
  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit). Union the keys if these land independently.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
